The `by omega` fails to prove `(if j.val < i.val then j.val else j.val + 1) < 5` because omega doesn't case-split on the `if`. The goal has the `if` expression in it. Need `split` or `by_cases` before omega... but the proof already does `by_cases h` AFTER the `if` is constructed, so the goal at that point is still `(if ... then ... else ...) < 5` — the `by_cases h` doesn't rewrite the goal's `if` automatically (only `simp [h]` or `split` would).

